  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements.</p><p>Statement I : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> are weakly attracted by magnetic field and are magnetized in the same direction as magnetic field.</p><p>Statement II :&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCl</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> are weakly magnetized in opposite direction to magnetic field.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer form the options given below</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are correct.",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct.",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;all have unpaired electrons so, they are paramagnetic,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>has</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>two</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>unpaired</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>electrons</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>according</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>to</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MOT</mi><mo>,</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>has</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>9</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>configuration</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>so</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>one</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>unpaired</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>electron</mi><mo>.</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>has</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>configuration</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>so</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>unpaired</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>electrons</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;Weakly attracted by magnetic field.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCl</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;does not have any unpaired electrons so they are diamagnetic,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Weakly repelled by magnetic field.</p></blockquote>"
  }
